er asks to \"start session\", \"log session\", \"begin turn\", \"update turn\", \"complete turn\", or \"query session history\"\n4: version: 0.1.0\n5: ---\n6: \n7: # Session Log Management\n8: \n9: ## Overview\n10: \n11: To manage agent session logs, use the `workflow.sessionlog.*` REPL command namespace through the plugin wrapper (`lib/repl-invoke.ps1` / `Invoke-McpPlugin.ps1`). Session logging captures agent activity, reasoning dialog, file operations, and design decisions as a structured audit trail.\n12: \n13: `workflow.sessionlog.*` is a plugin workflow/REPL namespace, not a literal native MCP tool namespace. Native McpServer `/mcp-transport` discovery uses names such as `sessionlog_*`, `todo_*`, and `requirements_*`; hosted-agent adapters may expose `mcp_session_*` aliases, and your agent's tool discovery may show configured MCP tools with native names such as `sessionlog_submit`, `todo_list`, and `requirements_generate`. Do not call this plugin unavailable solely because `workflow.*` names are absent from generic MCP discovery.\n14: \n15: `workflow.*` result envelopes may include `deprecated: true`. This is success metadata that tells callers the workflow namespace is legacy-compatible and should migrate toward the canonical `client.*` surface where available; it is not a failure signal and is not a reason to use raw REST. Treat an empty `workflow.sessionlog.queryHistory` result as a valid no-match result, not as an inert wrapper. Re-check the workspace current directory, the explicit `agent` or `sourceType`, and local plugin cache/session state through the wrapper before reporting history as unavailable.\n16: \n17: This skill covers manual operations, history queries, and the full lifecycle for agents that need direct control.\n18: \n19: ## Preferred Workflow\n20: \n21: For most work sessions:\n22: \n23: 1. Bootstrap session logging once.\n24: 2. Open or resume the session.\n25: 3. On each user request, begin a turn.\n26: 4. Consult current session/task state before asking the user for context.\n27: 5. Update the turn with relevant files, decisions, and actions.\n28: 6. Complete the turn after verification, or record failure if blocked.\n29: \n30: ## Running the Workflow Methods\n31: \n32: When the plugin's hooks (in `hooks/`) are active, most session management is automated and you do not need to drive it by hand. When hooks are not active for your agent, drive the lifecycle yourself through the plugin wrapper, never by hand-piping envelopes to REPL stdio:\n33: \n34: ```pwsh\n35: pwsh -NoProfile -File \"<plugin-root>/lib/repl-invoke.ps1\" -Method <method> -ParamsYaml @'\n36: <yaml params>\n37: '@\n38: ```\n39: \n40: The equivalent function form is `Invoke-McpPlugin.ps1 \"<method>\" \"<yaml params>\"`. For a one-shot bootstrap plus session open, prefer `<plugin-root>/lib/session-start.ps1 <workspace-path>`.\n41: \n42: The YAML envelope blocks in this skill document the wire contract each method maps to. Pass the `params:` body to the wrapper; it wraps it in the request envelope, validates documented params, and emits single-line JSON to REPL stdio for you. If you bypass the wrapper for diagnostics and write to REPL stdio directly, send one single-line JSON request envelope per message, never formatted YAML.\n43: \n44: Why the wrapper and not raw stdio:\n45: \n46: - `workflow.sessionlog.beginTurn` and `openSession` are not server routes. Calling them raw returns `method_invocation_error` / `method_not_found`. The wrapper treats them as local no-ops and tracks turn state in `cache/current-turn.yaml`.\n47: - Persisting a turn goes through `client.SessionLog.SubmitAsync`, which is strict: `actions[].order` must be an unquoted integer (`order: 1`, never `order: \"1\"`) or you get `JSON value could not be converted to System.Int32`. The wrapper builds the envelope with correct types.\n48: - There is no `session.init` method. Bootstrap with `workflow.sessionlog.bootstrap` only.\n49: \n50: ## Identifier Naming Conventions\n51: \n52: ### Session IDs\n53: \n54: Format: `<Agent>-<yyyyMMddTHHmmssZ>-<suffix>`\n55: \n56: Regex: `^[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9]*-\\d{8}T\\d{6}Z-[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$`\n57: \n58: - Agent name must be PascalCase (e.g. `YourAgent`)\n59: - Timestamp must be ISO 8601 compact UTC: `yyyyMMddTHHmmssZ`\n60: - Suffix must be lowercase kebab-case: `feature-auth`, `bugfix-timeout`\n61: \n62: Valid examples: `YourAgent-20260409T120000Z-implement-auth`, `YourAgent-20260304T113901Z-refactor-session`\n63: \n64: Invalid: `youragent-20260409T120000Z-task` (lowercase agent), `YourAgent-20260304-feature` (missing time component)\n65: \n66: ### Request IDs\n67: \n68: Format: `req-<yyyyMMddTHHmmssZ>-<slugOrOrdinal>`\n69: \n70: Regex: `^req-\\d{8}T\\d{6}Z-[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$`\n71: \n72: Valid examples: `req-20260409T120001Z-add-jwt-001`, `req-20260409T120002Z-query-todos`\n73: \n74: Invalid: `request-20260409T120001Z-task` (wrong prefix), `req-20260409-task` (missing time)\n75: \n76: ## Session Lifecycle\n77: \n78: ### Step 1 - Bootstrap (once per process lifetime)\n79: \n80: Bootstrap initializes the session log subsystem. This operation is idempotent:\n81: \n82: ```yaml\n83: type: request\n84: payload:\n85:   requestId: req-20260409T120000Z-bootstrap-001\n86:   method: workflow.sessionlog.bootstrap\n87:   params: {}\n88: ```\n89: \n90: ```yaml\n91: type: result\n92: payload:\n93:   requestId: req-20260409T120000Z-bootstrap-001\n94:   result:\n95:     initialized: true\n96: ```\n97: \n98: ### Step 2 - Open Session\n99: \n100: To create a new session record at the start of a work session:\n101: \n102: ```yaml\n103: type: request\n104: payload:\n105:   requestId: req-20260409T120001Z-open-001\n106:   method: workflow.sessionlog.openSession\n107:   params:\n108:     agent: YourAgent\n109:     sessionId: YourAgent-20260409T120001Z-implement-auth\n110:     title: Implement JWT authentication\n111:     model: <model-id>\n112: ```\n113: \n114: ```yaml\n115: type: result\n116: payload:\n117:   requestId: req-20260409T120001Z-open-001\n118:   result:\n119:     sessionId: YourAgent-20260409T120001Z-implement-auth\n120:     started: 2026-04-09T12:00:01Z\n121: ```\n122: \n123: ### Step 3 - Begin Turn (once per user message)\n124: \n125: To start a new turn before working on a user request:\n126: \n127: ```yaml\n128: type: request\n129: payload:\n130:   requestId: req-20260409T120002Z-begin-001\n131:   method: workflow.sessionlog.beginTurn\n132:   params:\n133:     requestId: req-20260409T120002Z-add-jwt-001\n134:     queryTitle: Add JWT authentication\n135:     queryText: Implement JWT token generation and validation for the API\n136: ```\n137: \n138: ```yaml\n139: type: result\n140: payload:\n141:   requestId: req-20260409T120002Z-begin-001\n142:   result:\n143:     turnRequestId: req-20260409T120002Z-add-jwt-001\n144:     status: in_progress\n145:     timestamp: 2026-04-09T12:00:02Z\n146: ```\n147: \n148: ### Step 4 - Update Turn\n149: \n150: To record interpretation, response summary, tags, and referenced files during work:\n151: \n152: ```yaml\n153: type: request\n154: payload:\n155:   requestId: req-20260409T120003Z-update-001\n156:   method: workflow.sessionlog.updateTurn\n157:   params:\n158:     response: Created TokenService and JwtValidator classes\n159:     interpretation: User wants JWT authentication with token generation and validation\n160:     tokenCount: 1250\n161:     tags:\n162:       - feature\n163:       - security\n164:       - FR-AUTH-001\n165:     contextList:\n166:       - src/Services/TokenService.cs\n167:       - src/Services/JwtValidator.cs\n168: ```\n169: \n170: ### Step 5 - Append Dialog\n171: \n172: To record reasoning steps, tool calls, observations, and decisions as the work progresses:\n173: \n174: ```yaml\n175: type: request\n176: payload:\n177:   requestId: req-20260409T120004Z-dialog-001\n178:   method: workflow.sessionlog.appendDialog\n179:   params:\n180:     dialogItems:\n181:       - timestamp: 2026-04-09T12:00:04Z\n182:         role: model\n183:         content: Analyzing authentication requirements and existing patterns...\n184:         category: reasoning\n185:       - timestamp: 2026-04-09T12:00:05Z\n186:         role: model\n187:         content: |\n188:           Decision: Use HS256 for JWT signing.\n189:           Rationale: Symmetric key simplifies key management for this internal service.\n190:           Alternatives: RS256 adds key distribution complexity without benefit here.\n191:         category: decision\n192: ```\n193: \n194: Valid `category` values: `reasoning`, `tool_call`, `tool_result`, `observation`, `decision`.\n195: \n196: Valid `role` values: `model`, `tool`, `system`, `user`.\n197: \n198: ### Step 6 - Append Actions\n199: \n200: To record file operations and other work artifacts:\n201: \n202: ```yaml\n203: type: request\n204: payload:\n205:   requestId: req-20260409T120005Z-actions-001\n206:   method: workflow.sessionlog.appendActions\n207:   params:\n208:     actions:\n209:       - order: 1\n210:         description: Created TokenService with JWT generation\n211:         type: create\n212:         status: completed\n213:         filePath: src/Services/TokenService.cs\n214:       - order: 2\n215:         description: Created JwtValidator for token validation\n216:         type: create\n217:         status: completed\n218:         filePath: src/Services/JwtValidator.cs\n219:       - order: 3\n220:         description: Chose HS256 for JWT signing (internal service, symmetric key)\n221:         type: design_decision\n222:         status: completed\n223:         filePath: \"\"\n224: ```\n225: \n226: Standard action `type` values: `edit`, `create`, `delete`, `design_decision`, `commit`, `pr_comment`, `issue_comment`, `web_reference`, `dependency_add`.\n227: \n228: `actions[].order` must be an unquoted integer (`order: 1`, never `order: \"1\"`).\n229: \n230: ### Step 7 - Complete Turn\n231: \n232: To finalize a turn as successfully completed (immutable after this call):\n233: \n234: ```yaml\n235: type: request\n236: payload:\n237:   requestId: req-20260409T120006Z-complete-001\n238:   method: workflow.sessionlog.completeTurn\n239:   params:\n240:     response: |\n241:       JWT authentication implemented:\n242:       - TokenService generates HS256-signed tokens\n243:       - JwtValidator validates and extracts claims\n244:       - Services registered in Startup.cs\n245:       - All unit tests passing\n246: ```\n247: \n248: ### Failing a Turn\n249: \n250: To mark a turn as failed with an error description:\n251: \n252: ```yaml\n253: type: request\n254: payload:\n255:   requestId: req-20260409T120007Z-fail-001\n256:   method: workflow.sessionlog.failTurn\n257:   params:\n258:     errorMessage: Unable to complete - missing System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt package\n259:     errorCode: dependency_missing\n260: ```\n261: \n262: Both `completeTurn` and `failTurn` produce an immutable terminal state. No further `updateTurn`, `appendDialog`, or `appendActions` calls are allowed on a completed or failed turn.\n263: \n264: ## Querying Session History\n265: \n266: To browse previous sessions for context continuity:\n267: \n268: ```yaml\n269: type: request\n270: payload:\n271:   requestId: req-20260409T120008Z-history-001\n272:   method: workflow.sessionlog.queryHistory\n273:   params:\n274:     agent: YourAgent\n275:     limit: 10\n276:     offset: 0\n277: ```\n278: \n279: ```yaml\n280: type: result\n281: payload:\n282:   requestId: req-20260409T120008Z-history-001\n283:   result:\n284:     sessions:\n285:       - agent: YourAgent\n286:         sessionId: YourAgent-20260409T120001Z-implement-auth\n287:         title: Implement JWT authentication\n288:         model: <model-id>\n289:         started: 2026-04-09T12:00:01Z\n290:         lastUpdated: 2026-04-09T12:30:00Z\n291:         status: completed\n292:         turnCount: 3\n293:         filesModifiedCount: 5\n294:         tags: [auth, jwt, security]\n295:     totalCount: 1\n296:     offset: 0\n297:     limit: 10\n298: ```\n299: \n300: Omit `agent` to query across all agents. Use `offset` and `limit` for pagination.\n301: \n302: ## Turn Lifecycle State Machine\n303: \n304: A turn transitions through these states only in forward order:\n305: \n306: 1. `in_progress` - created via `beginTurn`, open for updates\n307: 2. `completed` - finalized via `completeTurn` (immutable)\n308: 3. `failed` - finalized via `failTurn` (immutable)\n309: \n310: Any attempt to call `updateTurn`, `appendDialog`, or `appendActions` on a `completed` or `failed` turn returns a `turn_immutable` error.\n311: \n312: ## Error Handling\n313: \n314: ```yaml\n315: type: error\n316: payload:\n317:   requestId: req-20260409T120003Z-update-001\n318:   code: turn_immutable\n319:   message: Turn is immutable (status: completed)\n320:   details:\n321:     turnRequestId: req-20260409T120002Z-add-jwt-001\n322:     currentStatus: completed\n323:     hint: Begin a new turn instead\n324: ```\n325: \n326: Common error codes:\n327: \n328: - `session_not_found`: no active session; call `openSession` first\n329: - `session_already_exists`: session ID already in use\n330: - `invalid_session_id`: session ID format violation\n331: - `invalid_request_id`: request ID format violation\n332: - `turn_not_found`: no active turn; call `beginTurn` first\n333: - `turn_already_exists`: turn with same request ID already exists\n334: - `turn_immutable`: cannot modify completed or failed turn\n335: \n336: ## Session Continuity After Restart\n337: \n338: After a server restart or agent reconnect:\n339: \n340: 1. Call `workflow.sessionlog.queryHistory` to review past sessions\n341: 2. Decide whether to continue in a new session referencing the previous one in the title, or to re-open fresh\n342: 3. Re-read `AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml` for the rotated API key before making any calls\n343: 4. Call `bootstrap` again (idempotent) then `openSession` for the new session\n344: \n345: ## Model-Authored Session Logging\n346: \n347: Plugins do not import local chat transcripts for normal session logging. The active model must write its own session log through `workflow.sessionlog.beginTurn`, `workflow.sessionlog.appendDialog`, `workflow.sessionlog.appendActions`, and `workflow.sessionlog.completeTurn` or `workflow.sessionlog.failTurn`.\n348: \n349: ### Turn Completion\n350: \n351: Plugin stop/final-response helpers may complete an active turn through `lib/repl-invoke.ps1`, but the turn payload must already be model-authored through the session-log workflow. The runtime builds request envelopes with PowerShell objects and serializers. Secret values (API keys, Bearer tokens) are redacted before logging.\n352: \n353: ### Subagent Logging\n354: \n355: Subagents are responsible for writing their own turns through the same session-log workflow. Parent or child models may include parent request IDs, agent names, and source metadata as tags or actions when those values are available, but plugin packages must not parse transcript files to populate session logs.\n356: \n357: ### Manual Recovery\n358: \n359: Manual recovery uses the normal `workflow.sessionlog.*` commands or non-plugin server-side transcript ingestion when explicitly invoked outside a plugin package. Plugins must not expose transcript ingestion helpers, skills, endpoint shortcuts, or parser forks.\n360: \n361: ### Non-Destructive Merge\n362: \n363: Server-side rich fields are never overwritten by sparse incoming values. The PowerShell session payload builder uses field-level merge: an empty incoming array never replaces a non-empty server-side array. This allows model-authored `completeTurn` calls to close turns safely after rich fields have already been captured through the session-log workflow.\n364: \n365: ### Secret Redaction\n366: \n367: The following patterns are redacted from model-authored session-log text before logging:\n368: \n369: - `X-Api-Key:` header values\n370: - `apiKey:` parameter values (20+ character strings)\n371: - `Bearer <token>` values\n372: - `Authorization:` header values\n373: \n374: ## Implementation Notes\n375: \n376: - Use `Invoke-McpPlugin.ps1` from `lib/repl-invoke.ps1` to build and dispatch envelopes.\n377: - Generate request IDs with the current UTC timestamp to guarantee uniqueness: `req-$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)-<slug>`.\n378: - Post `beginTurn` before starting any work on a user request; post `completeTurn` or `failTurn` after work ends. Never defer these calls.\n379: - Log all design decisions in `appendDialog` with `category: decision` AND in `appendActions` with `type: design_decision`.\n380: - Record all web sources consulted as actions with `type: web_reference` and include the URL in the description.\n381: - At approximately every 10 interactions, verify all turns are persisted and all design decisions are captured before continuing.\nFILE: /home/sharpninja/github/vice-sharp/docs/receipts/hv/20261020T122200-plan-nativerestore-001-gpt61sol/request.jsonl (1 lines)\n1: {\"timestampLocal\":\"2026-10-20T12:25:57\",\"workspacePath\":\"/home/sharpninja/github/vice-sharp\",\"gate\":\"PLAN-NATIVERESTORE-001 plan approval (Phase D of GOAL-LOCKSTEP-REMEDIATION-001)\",\"classification\":\"class-1 plan review before execution\",\"reviewer\":{\"agent\":\"codex-cli\",\"cliVersion\":\"codex-cli 0.162.1\",\"model\":\"gpt-6.1-sol\",\"effort\":\"max\",\"family\":\"OpenAI GPT\"},\"implementer\":{\"agent\":\"ClaudeCode\",\"model\":\"claude-fable-5-1\",\"effort\":\"high\"},\"parentSessionId\":\"ClaudeCode-20261020T015046Z-plugin-session\",\"parentRequestId\":\"req-20261020T172116Z-prompt-6c6d\",\"executable\":\"/home/sharpninja/.local/share/mise/installs/codex/latest/bin/codex\",\"executableSha256\":\"628E35487D888A28F0427FC37501DA529DD3D81FCBAD7A2C3421C1E8670D92E1\",\"arguments\":[\"exec\",\"--json\",\"-m\",\"gpt-6.1-sol\",\"-c\",\"model_reasoning_effort=\\\"max\\\"\",\"-c\",\"approval_policy=\\\"never\\\"\",\"-s\",\"workspace-write\",\"-C\",\"/home/sharpninja/github/vice-sharp\",\"-o\",\"/home/sharpninja/github/vice-sharp/docs/receipts/hv/20261020T122200-plan-nativerestore-001-gpt61sol/last-message.md\",\"-\"],\"promptPath\":\"/home/sharpninja/github/vice-sharp/docs/receipts/hv/20261020T122200-plan-nativerestore-001-gpt61sol/prompt.md\",\"prompt\":\"# Hostile validation: PLAN-NATIVERESTORE-001 (Phase D plan) before execution\\n\\nYou are the independent hostile reviewer for this round: GPT-6.1-Sol at reasoning effort max through the Codex CLI on LAB-OMARCHY, workspace /home/sharpninja/github/vice-sharp, branch develop. The implementer is a Claude session (claude-fable-5-1-high@ClaudeCode); you are a different agent family by the operator's rule. This is a review of a plan before any of its steps execute; nothing under native/vice has changed, and nothing may change during your review.\\n\\nFIRST: run the add-profile skill exactly as its SKILL.md says (read every non-skill *.md under /home/sharpninja/.claude/profile in full; currently PROFILE-MERGED.md), then read the ENTIRE AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml at the workspace root, every line, without printing credentials or API keys. Bootstrap your own supported plugin (mcpserver-codex-plugin, the marker's agent_plugins contract, root /home/sharpninja/github/mcpserver-codex-plugin; verify with Invoke-CodexMcpPlugin.ps1 -Command Status) and open your own review session-log turn through it, titled with a short summary of this request, linked to the parent ids in this directory's request.jsonl (parentSessionId, parentRequestId). Do not repair hooks or environment, do not replay queues, do not cancel historical turns, do not invoke nested reviewers, do not substitute the model. There are no time or turn bounds on this review.\\n\\nMANDATORY live progress: before analysis and at meaningful checkpoints, emit a TEXT JSON object into your output with timestampLocal (a measured sortable local date and time, never estimated), numeric completionPercent and etaSeconds (null only if genuinely unknown). These are your own reports, not deadlines; do not backfill them at the end.\\n\\nOperator rulings verbatim (treat as acceptance criteria): D4 (2026-10-19): native restoration approved; \\\"Build artifacts are not code dirt. They should be gitignored.\\\"; \\\"restore native/vice means revert the tracked modifications after preserving them, and exclude the build output through git ignore rules instead of deleting it\\\". D3: \\\"No HV until your current scope of work is complete and passes 98/98 holistic self-assessment\\\", clarified \\\"This is a remediation/cleanup phase, not new code\\\"; on 2026-10-20T12:21 the operator stated that plans are hostile-validated under the standing rules, which is why this round exists. 2026-10-20T10:40: \\\"Wait for the Windows trace results first\\\" before Phase D step 1. 10:53: \\\"Before beginning phase D implementation, ensure both omarchy and legion2 have latest desktop build installed via nuke.\\\" 10:57 answers: R1 \\\"B: .gitmodules ignore = untracked only\\\"; R2 and R3 \\\"A: retire it now\\\"; R4 \\\"Yes, exclude and keep\\\"; R5 \\\"Yes, add in D2\\\". 12:09: \\\"Hold until LEGION2 reports\\\". Standing rules: never move a file (copy, verify by hash, retain the original until the operator clears deletion); never force-push; PowerShell only, no Python, no Node; every script analyzer-checked and dry-run with -WhatIf; BDPv4 mocks first for every behavior change; VICE is immutable (never edit, patch, generate into, clean or restore native/vice outside this plan's approved steps).\\n\\nRead end to end, rehashing every pin in input-pins.json before you start and disclosing any drift: docs/plans/PLAN-NATIVERESTORE-001.md (the subject), docs/receipts/handoff/HANDOFF.lockstep-plan.md section 4 Phase D, docs/receipts/handoff/HANDOFF.lockstep-plan.v2.md sections 4 and 11, docs/plans/PLAN-VICE-IMMUTABLE-001.md (Phase 0 and Phase 3), docs/receipts/native-vice/20261004T090000-0500-preexisting-delta/README.md and its patch, docs/