r are removed from the tree (their last versions remain in git history and in the Phase 0 receipt's context); `native/build-vice-observer.ps1` is the only native builder; the suites that P/Invoke the shim (`SnapshotResume*`, `SnapshotRunLogParity`, `Vic20SnapshotRoundTrip`, `Vic20NativeLockstepTests`) stay in the categories the Nuke `Test` filter already excludes until Phase E rebinds them to the observer binaries. B: keep the shim sources and scripts in the tree, inert, until Phase E has replaced every consumer. Either way no shim is built in Phase D.\n38: - R3 Linux shell launchers (`build-vice-shim.sh`, `build-vice-shim-xvic.sh`): removal under R2 A, or thin PowerShell launchers under R2 B (operator rule: PowerShell only).\n39: - R4 LEGION2's 2,527 untracked entries and the injected header: exclude (R1 A) and leave in place; deletion only on Payton's explicit clearance per the never-move-a-file rule. Confirm.\n40: - R5 Solution and Nuke: add the three native-safe projects to `ViceSharp.slnx` and to the Nuke `Test` target now (handoff step 2), so every gate from here runs them without a per-project command. Confirm.\n41: \n42: ## 4. Steps (BDPv4, mocks first where behavior changes; no hostile validation inside the phase, D3)\n43: \n44: - D-pre Precondition (Payton, 2026-10-20T10:53, verbatim: \"Before beginning phase D implementation, ensure both omarchy and legion2 have latest desktop build installed via nuke.\"): on each machine the desktop app is built and installed from the current `develop` head through the Nuke deployment target of that platform (the Linux user-local deployment on LAB-OMARCHY; `InstallMsi` on PAYTON-LEGION2), with the receipt (target, commit, installed version, exact command output) recorded before D0 starts. Class-2 operator action, not BDPv4 work.\n45: \n46: - D0 Measure and preserve, both machines, read only except for the receipt. Record the gitlink and checked-out SHA, `git -C native/vice diff` (full patch, SHA256), `status --porcelain=