{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"& './docs/receipts/hv/20261020T122200-plan-nativerestore-001-gpt61sol/Read-ReviewEvidence.ps1' -Operation Read -Paths 'docs/receipts/handoff/HANDOFF.lockstep-plan.md' -StartLine 67 -LineCount 95; & './docs/receipts/hv/20261020T122200-plan-nativerestore-001-gpt61sol/Read-ReviewEvidence.ps1' -Operation Read -Paths 'docs/receipts/handoff/HANDOFF.lockstep-plan.v2.md' -StartLine 62 -LineCount 43\"","aggregated_output":"FILE: docs/receipts/handoff/HANDOFF.lockstep-plan.md (200 lines)\n67: ## 4. The plan\n68: \n69: Phases are sequential unless stated. Each lists entry, work, exit, and the requirements and tests it serves. \"HV\" means the Opus 5.5 max gate described above.\n70: \n71: ### Phase A: Measured Windows baseline and decisions (no product code)\n72: \n73: Entry: this handoff, `develop` at `d00e8c5`, decisions D1 to D9 answered or explicitly deferred by Payton.\n74: \n75: Work:\n76: 1. Re-run the three native-safe suites unfiltered in Release through PowerShell.MCP (`ViceSharp.OracleContract.Tests`, `ViceSharp.VsfCompatibility.Tests`, `ViceSharp.NativeClockProbe.Tests`) with native before/after inventory capture; record counts against the Oct 8 figures (87, 199, 69).\n77: 2. Run the existing TestHarness lockstep and acceptance filters once as a diagnostic against the current prebuilt dirty shim, without rebuilding it (do not invoke `Vice.Native.proj`; if the harness build cannot avoid it, stop and report rather than build). Targets: `LockstepValidationTests`, `Vic20NativeLockstepTests`, `Vic20HalfCycleComparatorTests`, `CpuVisiblePcTimingTests`, `X64ScVariantLockstepTests`, every `Fr*AcceptanceTests` class, `Category=Determinism`. Identify the five CPU/NMI failures from PR7 by name. Label all of this \"diagnostic oracle\".\n78: 3. Record the baseline as `docs/receipts/lockstep/{yyyyMMddTHHmmss}-phase-a-baseline/` with commands, TRX, counts, native inventory, marker hash, and the decision answers.\n79: 4. Link `PLAN-ARCHVIC20-001` to `FR-VIC20-*` and this handoff through the TODO wrapper; add a checkpoint to `PLAN-VICEORACLE-001` naming this file. No other TODO or requirement mutation.\n80: \n81: Exit: baseline receipt exists; decisions recorded in the session turn; no HV required (operational class).\n82: \n83: ### Phase B: Accept the native-safe mock gate (immutable Phase 1)\n84: \n85: Entry: Phase A receipt.\n86: \n87: Work: repin the 826-input packet from `docs/receipts/hv/20261008T143538-0500-opus-remediation-packet/` against the current tree, disclose every changed input, then launch one Opus 5.5 max review of the whole Phase 1 scope (the three mock projects, the 16 draft findings and their dispositions, the shared fixtures, stdio mock contract, and the Oct 8 evidence corrections). Remediate findings inside the mock projects only; no production code.\n88: \n89: Exit: AGREE 98/98, zero FAIL/UNKNOWN, full verdict read back; the three suites unfiltered green; native inventory unchanged; `PLAN-VICEORACLE-001` task 2 done. Serves `FR-VICE-001` AC1 to AC4, `TR-VICE-ORACLE-001` AC1 to AC5, `TEST-VICE-001` AC1 to AC4, `TR-CYCLE-001` AC4 at contract level.\n90: \n91: ### Phase C: External bus observer and cycle control for both machines (immutable Phase 2)\n92: \n93: Entry: Phase B accepted.\n94: \n95: Work, in the plan's mechanism order (public interfaces, external process control, link-time interposition outside both source trees), on the separate materialization only:\n96: 1. Specify the observation record (half-cycle index, PHI1/PHI2, AEC, BA, access kind read/write/idle/dummy, address, data, interrupt stage, stolen-cycle flag, clock) as a mock-first contract in `ViceSharp.OracleContract.Tests` and `ViceSharp.NativeClockProbe.Tests`, with negative controls for every missing field; mock gate green; HV.\n97: 2. Bind the stdio diagnostic adapter (the 19 mock-contract cases in `StdioAdapterContractTests`) to a