. Record the gitlink SHA, checked-out SHA, tracked diff, untracked source inventory, wrapper binaries, and hashes.\n79: 2. Save the meaningful existing source delta as a read-only receipt outside `native/vice`. Separate generated build output from human-authored source changes.\n80: 3. Mark every test result produced from the patched native build as diagnostic only, not immutable-target acceptance evidence.\n81: 4. Do not delete or restore anything in this phase.\n82: 5. Persist the exact pending `TR-VSFLOCKSTEP-RESUME-001` correction and outage evidence in the Codex session turn through supported v4 session-log failsafe. This preserves the decision but does not claim the requirement database was mutated.\n83: 6. After service recovery, drain the session-log failsafe, update the TR through `workflow.requirements.updateTr`, prove primary readback, regenerate requirement projections through `workflow.requirements.generateDocument`, and rerun traceability before the mock-validation phase.\n84: \n85: Current preservation receipt: `docs/receipts/native-vice/20261004T090000-0500-preexisting-delta/`. Its tracked patch passes reverse-apply validation against the dirty checkout, and its copied `vice-shim-runtime.h` hash matches the source file.\n86: \n87: Exit gate:\n88: \n89: - Preservation receipt is complete and independently readable.\n90: - If MCP persistence genuinely fails, preserve the complete session/HV result through the operator-authorized supported failsafe, with exact pending paths, SHA-256 values, and `PrimaryReadback: false` disclosed. No unaccounted corrupt or quarantined record may be presented as successfully saved or replayed.\n91: - Before Phase 1 begins, `TR-VSFLOCKSTEP-RESUME-001` is updated in the primary requirement store, read back with both corrected ACs pending, and generated projections no longer mandate the patch. Reconcile pending session/HV records across every workspace agent queue, not only Codex: valid records must be safely drained and read back; corrupt cross-session records must not be replayed into historical turns. On 2026-10-07 the operator explicitly authorized preserving and quarantining five such hook-generated records. Their retained bytes, matching backup/quarantine hashes, reason files, zero replay count, and unchanged primary sessions are recorded in `docs/receipts/hv/20261007T125315-0500-failsafe-quarantine/verification.json`. This is an approved quarantine disposition, not a claim that those records were replayed. Historical quarantine artifacts remain evidence, not active pending writes.\n92: - Subsequent queue reconciliation: `978b`, `7058`, and `40a8` were safely replayed with primary readbacks under `docs/receipts/hv/20261007T163600-0500-phase0-opus-remediation/`. Additional stale snapshot `7dc1` received a separate operator approval and supported quarantine, not replay; `docs/receipts/hv/20261007T171002-0500-approved-7dc1-quarantine/verification.json` proves its bytes preserved, target turn still completed and deeply equal, zero active pending records, and seven total retained quarantine records (the five historical cancellations, older triage `2b86`, and `7dc1`). Do not discard or replay these retained records.\n93: - Hostile review returns AGREE with accuracy and completeness at least 98 and no FAIL or UNKNOWN.\n94: \nFILE: docs/plans/PLAN-VICE-IMMUTABLE-001.md (218 lines)\n144: ## Phase 2: Wrapper-only feasibility proof\n145: \n146: Implement the smallest external proof that immutable xvic can be controlled and observed without source changes. The proof may not use the dirty working checkout as its oracle. Materialize the pinned commit into a separate initially clean local source tree outside `native/vice`, record its tree identity and complete preflight status, and follow the pinned VICE Team build procedure. Per operator approval on 2026-10-08, required in-source build generation is allowed only in that separate materialization. Record generated files separately and verify every original tracked source byte and commit remain unchanged. Evaluate wrapper mechanisms in this order:\n147: \n148: 1. Existing public VICE monitor, trace, history, snapshot, and exported interfaces.\n149: 2. External process control around the stock executable.\n150: 3. Link-time symbol wrapping or function-table interposition performed entirely by wrapper build inputs outside both `native/vice` and the clean materialized source tree, with byte-identical target sources and unchanged target semantics.\n151: \n152: The same boundary applies to recovered snapshot compatibility. A dedicated external adapter must prove that validated v1.2 `MAINCPU` input gains only the absent v1.3 and v1.4 fields, v1.3 gains only the absent v1.4 field, v1.4 passes through byte-for-byte, all following bytes and module ordering remain unchanged, and malformed or unsupported layouts fail closed before immutable VICE reads the temporary copy. `native/patches/vice-shim-runtime.patch` is preservation evidence only and may not participate in a build.\n153: \n154: The proof must obtain the real executed CPU bus address, data, read/write direction, dummy/real classification, clock position, interrupt stage, and stolen-cycle state needed by Slice 3c. It must also support deterministic cycle-boundary control.\n155: \n156: If the pinned VICE source cannot be materialized and built using the approved upstream procedure without changing original source bytes or writing under `native/vice`, or immutable VICE cannot expose a required observation through the allowed wrapper mechanisms, stop with a named blocker. Do not patch VICE or weaken the comparator. Required build generation in the separate materialization is permitted by the 2026-10-08 operator approval and must have its own inventory.\n157: \n158: Exit gate:\n159: \n160: - The full applicable current-plus-prior suite, including wrapper and legacy v1.2/v1.3/v1.4 snapshot-compatibility proofs, has failed 0, skipped 0, and aborted 0. Focused filters are diagnostic only.\n161: - The separate pinned source materialization is initially clean; its commit and every original tracked source byte remain unchanged after the proof. Required upstream-generated build artifacts have a separate path/hash/producer-command inventory and are not mislabeled as source edits or as zero untracked files.\n162: - The dirty `native/vice` checkout is byte-for-byte unchanged by the proof.\n163: - Hostile green-gate AGREE at 98/98 or higher with zero FAIL and UNKNOWN.\n164: \n165: ## Phase 3: Migrate or reject the existing native modifications\n166: \n167: For each of the 12 tracked source changes and the injected runtime header, classify it as:\n168: \n169: - Observation/control logic to rehome in an external wrapper.\n170: - Legacy snapshot normalization to rehome in the external compatibility adapter, with exact v1.2/v1.3/v1.4 fixture coverage.\n171: - Behavior correction that belongs in managed ViceSharp.\n172: - Target modification that must be rejected from the oracle.\n173: \n174: After the preservation receipt and wrapper feasibility proof are accepted, restore the `native/vice` tracked checkout to the pinned commit and remove only paths from the preserved untracked inventory after classifying them as generated output or injected source. Future build output must stay outside the submodule. Broad reset or cleanup commands remain forbidden. This restoration is destructive and begins only under the operator's 2026-10-04 approval and after the hostile gates above agree.\n175: \n176: Exit gate:\n177: \n178: - Recorded and checked-out gitlink SHAs match.\n179: - `git -C native/vice diff --exit-code` succeeds.\n180: - `git -C native/vice status --porcelain=v1 -uall` returns no entries.\n181: - No generated output, injected source, or wrapper input under `native/vice` participates in the oracle build.\n182: - Wrapper and managed replacements pass the full applicable current-plus-prior suite with failed 0, skipped 0, and aborted 0. Focused tests do not advance this gate.\n183: - Hostile green-gate AGREE at 98/98 or higher with zero FAIL and UNKNOWN.\n184: \n185: ## Phase 4: Resume xvic lockstep Slice 3c\n186: \n187: Extend only the existing `LockstepValidator`. Compare managed and immutable xvic on every required half-cycle for:\n188: \n189: - A, X, Y, S, P, and PC.\n190: - Opcode and micro-op phase.\n191: - Real bus address, data, and read/write direction.\n192: - Dummy cycle versus real access.\n193: - IRQ and NMI pipeline stage.\n194: - Stolen-cycle state.\n195: \n196: All native inputs come from the accepted external wrapper. Managed behavior changes to match VICE. The native target remains untouched.\n197: \n198: Exit gate:\n199: \n200: - The full applicable current-plus-prior suite, including comparator fixtures, native wrapper tests, and `REAL-C64-PHI2-AEC-001`, passes with failed 0, skipped 0, and aborted 0. Focused filters are diagnostic only.\n201: - C64 idle pins remain green when shared CPU or clock code changes.\n202: - Clean-target proof is attached to every native-backed receipt.\n203: - Hostile green-gate AGREE at 98/98 or higher with zero FAIL and UNKNOWN.\n204: \n205: ## Phase 5: Resume the remaining approved plan\n206: \n207: Continue the original Phase 3 repair pairs and Phase 4 settings work only after Phase 4 above is accepted. Every native-backed phase repeats clean-target preflight and provenance capture.\n208: \n209: ## Whole-plan exit additions\n210: \n211: The handoff completion plan cannot finish until:\n212: \n213: - `FR-VICE-001`, `TR-VICE-ORACLE-001`, and `TEST-VICE-001` have executable evidence for every AC.\n214: - Native VICE acceptance evidence comes from the pinned unmodified target.\n215: - All required wrapper capabilities exist outside `native/vice` or the plan stops at an explicit immutable-target blocker.\n216: - Primary MCP readback proves the corrected `TR-VSFLOCKSTEP-RESUME-001`; no requirement projection or active plan instructs an executor to apply the legacy patch.\n217: - Every executable phase exit has retained full applicable current-plus-prior suite evidence with zero failures, skips, and aborts. A missing capability or other named blocker leaves the goal incomplete; recording it is not an alternative completion condition.\n218: - The final hostile review agrees at accuracy and completeness at least 98 with zero FAIL and UNKNOWN.\nFILE: docs/receipts/native-vice/20261004T090000-0500-preexisting-delta/native-vice-tracked.patch (599 lines)\n1: diff --git a/vice/src/c64/c64cpusc.c b/vice/src/c64/c64cpusc.c\n2: index 5971a3c9d3..3ee311afbf 100644\n3: --- a/vice/src/c64/c64cpusc.c\n4: +++ b/vice/src/c64/c64cpusc.c\n5: @@ -32,6 +32,10 @@\n6:  #include \"monitor.h\"\n7:  #include \"vicii-cycle.h\"\n8:  \n9: +#ifdef VICE_SHIM_HOSTED\n10: +#include \"../vice-shim-runtime.h\"\n11: +#endif\n12: +\n13:  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */\n14:  \n15:  /* Global clock counter.  */\n16: @@ -44,11 +48,32 @@ CLOCK maincpu_clk_limit = 0L;\n17:  /* Mask: BA low */\n18:  int maincpu_ba_low_flags = 0;\n19:  \n20: +#ifdef VICE_SHIM_HOSTED\n21: +/* Hosted build (ViceSharp): after the normal per-cycle accounting, publish the\n22: +   CPU register file to the shim, let the host pause/stop at this cycle\n23: +   boundary, then re-import in case the host adjusted state. A stop request\n24: +   unwinds maincpu_mainloop() (return) so the hosting thread regains control.\n25: +   EXPORT_REGISTERS()/IMPORT_REGISTERS() are in scope here because CLK_INC()\n26: +   only expands inside the 6510dtvcore.c body, after those macros are defined. */\n27: +#define CLK_INC()                                      \\\n28: +    do {                                               \\\n29: +        interrupt_delay();                             \\\n30: +        maincpu_clk++;                                 \\\n31: +        maincpu_ba_low_flags &= ~MAINCPU_BA_LOW_VICII; \\\n32: +        maincpu_ba_low_flags |= vicii_cycle();         \\\n33: +        EXPORT_REGISTERS();                            \\\n34: +        if (vice_shim_cycle_checkpoint()) {            \\\n35: +            return;                                    \\\n36: +        }                                              \\\n37: +        IMPORT_REGISTERS();                            \\\n38: +    } while (0)\n39: +#else\n40:  #define CLK_INC()                                  \\\n41:      interrupt_delay();                             \\\n42:      maincpu_clk++;                                 \\\n43:      maincpu_ba_low_flags &= ~MAINCPU_BA_LOW_VICII; \\\n44:      maincpu_ba_low_flags |= vicii_cycle()\n45: +#endif\n46:  \n47:  \n48:  /* Skip cycle implementation */\n49: diff --git a/vice/src/drive/drive-snapshot.c b/vice/src/drive/drive-snapshot.c\n50: index 7417f7e60b..caf808abae 100644\n51: --- a/vice/src/drive/drive-snapshot.c\n52: +++ b/vice/src/drive/drive-snapshot.c\n53: @@ -314,9 +314,13 @@ int drive_snapshot_read_module(snapshot_t *s)\n54:      char snap_module_name[8];\n55:      uint32_t rotation_table_ptr[NUM_DISK_UNITS];\n56:      int has_tde[NUM_DISK_UNITS];\n57: -    CLOCK attach_clk[NUM_DISK_UNITS];\n58: -    CLOCK detach_clk[NUM_DISK_UNITS];\n59: -    CLOCK attach_detach_clk[NUM_DISK_UNITS];\n60: +    /* Zero-init: these are written only inside the per-unit if (has_tde[unr])\n61: +       block below, but copied unconditionally into drive_t for every unit whose\n62: +       type != DRIVE_TYPE_NONE. A has_tde=0 restore would otherwise copy in\n63: +       uninitialized stack; 0 is the fresh-boot baseline (drive_init, drive.c). */\n64: +    CLOCK attach_clk[NUM_DISK_UNITS] = {0};\n65: +    CLOCK detach_clk[NUM_DISK_UNITS] = {0};\n66: +    CLOCK attach_detach_clk[NUM_DISK_UNITS] = {0};\n67:      int sync_factor;\n68:      drive_t *drive;\n69:      diskunit_context_t *unit;\n70: diff --git a/vice/src/drive/drivecpu.c b/vice/src/drive/drivecpu.c\n71: index 493b92ab5c..fda4103248 100644\n72: --- a/vice/src/drive/drivecpu.c\n73: +++ b/vice/src/drive/drivecpu.c\n74: @@ -188,6 +188,10 @@ void drivecpu_reset_clk(diskunit_context_t *drv)\n75:      drv->cpu->last_clk = maincpu_clk;\n76:      drv->cpu->last_exc_cycles = 0;\n77:      drv->cpu->stop_clk = 0;\n78: +    /* cycle_accum is part of the derived clock state re-anchored here; leaving\n79: +       it stale phase-shifts the drive CPU on any reset not followed by a\n80: +       snapshot restore (the snapshot path re-writes it immediately after). */\n81: +    drv->cpu->cycle_accum = 0;\n82:  }\n83:  \n84:  /* called by drive_reset() (via machine_specific_reset()) */\n85: diff --git a/vice/src/drive/drivecpu65c02.c b/vice/src/drive/drivecpu65c02.c\n86: index 7da8730650..b2dc44a130 100644\n87: --- a/vice/src/drive/drivecpu65c02.c\n88: +++ b/vice/src/drive/drivecpu65c02.c\n89: @@ -170,6 +170,10 @@ void drivecpu65c02_reset_clk(diskunit_context_t *drv)\n90:      drv->cpu->last_clk = maincpu_clk;\n91:      drv->cpu->last_exc_cycles = 0;\n92:      drv->cpu->stop_clk = 0;\n93: +    /* Mirror drivecpu_reset_clk: re-anchor the fractional cycle accumulator so\n94: +       a reset without a following snapshot restore does not leave it stale\n95: +       (1581/2000/4000/CMDHD drives). */\n96: +    drv->cpu->cycle_accum = 0;\n97:  }\n98:  \n99:  void drivecpu65c02_reset(diskunit_context_t *drv)\n100: diff --git a/vice/src/mainc64cpu.c b/vice/src/mainc64cpu.c\n101: index 357b27452b..ce0cc5052a 100644\n102: --- a/vice/src/mainc64cpu.c\n103: +++ b/vice/src/mainc64cpu.c\n104: @@ -56,6 +56,10 @@\n105:  #include \"traps.h\"\n106:  #include \"types.h\"\n107:  \n108: +#ifdef VICE_SHIM_HOSTED\n109: +#include \"vice-shim-runtime.h\"\n110: +#endif\n111: +\n112:  #ifndef EXIT_FAILURE\n113:  #define EXIT_FAILURE 1\n114:  #endif\n115: @@ -196,7 +200,24 @@ inline static void check_ba(void)\n116:      if (maincpu_ba_low_flags) {\n117:          CLOCK old_maincpu_clk = maincpu_clk;\n118:  \n119: +#ifdef VICE_SHIM_HOSTED\n120: +        /* steal_cycle