{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -NoProfile -Command \"& './docs/receipts/hv/20261020T122200-plan-nativerestore-001-gpt61sol/Read-ReviewEvidence.ps1' -Operation Read -Paths 'docs/receipts/handoff/HANDOFF.lockstep-plan.v2.md' -StartLine 167 -LineCount 53; & './docs/receipts/hv/20261020T122200-plan-nativerestore-001-gpt61sol/Read-ReviewEvidence.ps1' -Operation Read -Paths 'docs/plans/PLAN-OBSERVER-001.md' -StartLine 5 -LineCount 17\"","aggregated_output":"FILE: docs/receipts/handoff/HANDOFF.lockstep-plan.v2.md (285 lines)\n167: ## 11. Decisions D1 to D9 answered by Payton, 2026-10-19, and the sequence chosen\n168: \n169: Answers were given in chat on 2026-10-19 (session-log turn `req-20261019T145757Z-prompt-aa4b`); facts below were measured at 2026-10-19T09:59:14 local on LAB-OMARCHY (`~/codex-dispatch/diag/d4d9-20261019/`). Where an answer changes a rule in sections 3 or 4, this section wins.\n170: \n171: - D1 (scope): \"I want all completed. You decide the sequence.\" Every item of the Grok whole-goal plan is in scope: the lockstep path, the dense session-log proof, the Phase 4 settings work, VSF Slices 6 and 7, and the RomM follow-ups. Sequence chosen below.\n172: - D2 (R0 delta): A. Apply the sixteen-record candidate (SHA256 `63386E92...55D702`) on PAYTON-LEGION2, then mirror to LAB-OMARCHY; Phase A step 6 below, before Phase E. Correction measured by the LEGION2 agent on 2026-10-19T10:46 (session `ClaudeCode-20261019T152439Z-plugin-session`, turn `req-20261019T152609Z-prompt-b96d`): the candidate's README makes application conditional on four things, and \"A\" alone does not name two of them. (a) Payton's approval of the exact 16-record, 9-row candidate; (b) explicit approval of the departure from locked decision 2, because `workflow.requirements.updateBatch` has no idempotency key (this handoff's earlier wording \"under the idempotency key\" was wrong: no such key exists); (c) an operator-attested exclusive-writer window recorded as an MCP decision; (d) R1 guard tests G01 to G18 mocks-first plus a coordinator before any write. Step 6 is blocked until Payton states (b) and (c) directly; (d) is implementation work inside step 6.\n173: - D3 (hostile validation): \"No HV until your current scope of work is complete and passes 98/98 holistic self-assessment\", clarified: \"This is a remediation/cleanup phase, not new code. I don't want time wasted on HV until remediation is code complete.\" The whole scope in this section is one remediation phase. No reviewer is launched at any gate inside it; each gate exits on the full applicable suite green plus a written self-assessment with accuracy and completeness ratings. One hostile review runs when remediation is code complete and self-assessed at 98/98. Until it returns AGREE, no TODO, requirement, acceptance criterion or plan step is marked done (profile 4.5 postponed, not waived).\n174: - D4 (native restoration): approved now; the Phase D entry reconfirmation is no longer required. Payton also stated that lockstep harnesses should already sit outside the submodule, and corrected the handoff's framing: \"Build artifacts are not code dirt. They should be gitignored.\" Observation on LAB-OMARCHY: the harness sources do sit outside (`native/vice-shim.c` 82,153 bytes, `native/vice-shim-vic20.c` 43,059, `native/vice-shim.h` 15,424, `tools/immutable-vice/clock-gate.c`, `clock-gate.h`, `clock-observer.c`), but the builds do not: `native/Vice.Native.proj` runs `build-vice-shim.ps1` on Windows only, the Linux `build-vice-shim.sh` builds inside `native/vice`, and `artifacts/immutable-vice/` is absent here (present on LEGION2 per section 2.2). Classification of the untracked entries (`~/codex-dispatch/scripts/Classify-PorcelainInventory.ps1` over the two Phase A inventories, 2026-10-19T10:15): LAB-OMARCHY 155 untracked, all autotools output (107 `.in`, the `configure` scripts, `.aclocal.out` and sibling logs, `compile`, `depcom