dnight automation is PAUSED. No quota loop or duplicate retry. Preserve N-16/N-17 disclosures: historical duplicate/unfinished hook turns, estimated interim reviewer timestamps and direct .NET receipt writes. Do not claim blanket workflow compliance.\n142: \n143: ## Current R0 candidate and supplements\nFILE: tools/immutable-vice/Invoke-ObserverEquivalence.ps1 (207 lines)\n1: <#\n2: .SYNOPSIS\n3: PLAN-OBSERVER-001 slice S3: equivalence runs of the observer binaries against the stock binaries.\n4: \n5: .DESCRIPTION\n6: For each machine (xvic, x64sc) and each cycle count, runs three headless, deterministic processes on the\n7: ROM-only reset workload (no media, VICE data directory from the hash-verified work tree, log colors off\n8: because the stock headless logger dereferences a null text when stdout is not a terminal and colors are on,\n9: dummy sound device, cycle limit, exit screenshot):\n10:   stock     the stock binary from the Make stage (no wrappers);\n11:   withheld  the observer binary with the bank-base fast path withheld (default);\n12:   keep      the observer binary with VICESHARP_FAST_PATH=keep (translate forwarded unchanged).\n13: The observer runs are gated: a permit stream of 'c' bytes feeds stdin, one per cycle. Evidence per run:\n14: exit code, SHA256 of the exit screenshot, counts of VICE_GATE, VICE_BUS access, access with kind missing,\n15: missing and foreign reports, translate events, STOP lines, and SHA256 of stdout and stderr.\n16: Equivalence claims checked here: exit screenshots byte-identical across the three runs; VICE_GATE counts\n17: equal between withheld and keep; no STOP, no missing or foreign report, no access with kind missing in the\n18: withheld run. Any difference is reported, never tolerated. Nothing under the materialization is touched.\n19: #>\n20: [CmdletBinding()]\n21: param(\n22:     [ValidateSet('x64sc', 'xvic', 'both')]\n23:     [string] $Machine = 'both',\n24:     [int[]] $Cycles = @(100000, 1000000),\n25:     [string]